/**
 * THE LAB PLATE
 *
 * A painted workshop, supplied rather than generated. Empty table, bare shelves,
 * clear floor, and — the thing that matters most — a window that is a genuinely
 * black opening and light that is flat and ambient.
 *
 * The first version of this plate had a summer sky painted in the window and a
 * hard sunbeam across the floor, which meant the room was a bright July noon
 * whatever the game said, and the code spent two layers arguing with it. This
 * one is lit by the weather instead: the view drops into the opening at its own
 * size, and the room brightens or dims with the day.
 *
 * Data URI, not public/: the game ships as one self-contained page whose CSP
 * blocks external images, so a file path works on the dev server and shows
 * nothing at all once published.
 *
 * Source at art/lab-source.jpg.
 */
